{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545720-m20-sorcerer-aspects-questions","id":1545720,"title":"[M20] Sorcerer Aspects Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-11T18:06:29-08:00","id":1545720,"title":"[M20] Sorcerer Aspects Questions","content":"Hey gang,<br /> So I'm reading Sorcerer 20th, and I find myself confused about Aspects rule. The difficulty of the roll is said to be the Path Level + 4, with the number of successes determined by the Aspects.<br /> &quot;When the hedge magician casts a spell, they must choose what level of each Aspect they want to include, with the default being zero \u2014 and therefore, no effect \u2014 in each. Hedge wizards can increase a given Aspect as high as the Path level, and the highest Aspect determines the level of the spell. When the spell is cast, it requires one success for each rank in each Aspect. Spells may contain any of the general Aspects listed here, modified and expanded by any Aspects listed in the Path\u2019s description. A hedge wizard only needs to purchase Aspects they require for the spell.&quot;<br /> So my questions are,<br /> 1. Is Path level simply the number of dots you have in the associated path? Or some other factor?<br /> 2. For paths that have listed Aspects, does that mean the number of Aspects listed is the minimum number of successes (Fortune has three listed in Aspects, so does it have a minimum of three successes)?<br /> 3. Each rank of an aspect (including rank 1 I assume), doesn't this mean that for Path's with a wide selection of aspects, aspects can reach into number of successes like 5 or even 6?<br /> 4. The optional rule of Simplified Aspects states that each Aspect can cost a single success, but says the cost is the increase of difficulty of the spell. But the difficulty is depending on the Path level?<br /> <br /> Feel free to correct any misunderstandings I have. Thanks in advanced for any help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28584-matter911","name":"Matter911","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T00:19:03-08:00","id":1545731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matter911</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545720-m20-sorcerer-aspects-questions#post1545720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is Path level simply the number of dots you have in the associated path?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matter911</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545720-m20-sorcerer-aspects-questions#post1545720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. For paths that have listed Aspects, does that mean the number of Aspects listed is the minimum number of successes (Fortune has three listed in Aspects, so does it have a minimum of three successes)?<br /> 3. Each rank of an aspect (including rank 1 I assume), doesn't this mean that for Path's with a wide selection of aspects, aspects can reach into number of successes like 5 or even 6?</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, yes. This is very impractical and imbalanced, the house rule I and many others seem to use is that the first success covers the first levels of each listed Aspect, similar to how it worked in Revised. Additional Aspect ranks beyond the first require the extra successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matter911</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545720-m20-sorcerer-aspects-questions#post1545720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. The optional rule of Simplified Aspects states that each Aspect can cost a single success, but says the cost is the increase of difficulty of the spell. But the difficulty is depending on the Path level?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that in order to cast an effect with a level 4 Aspect, you need to cast at Path level 4. In Revised each Path had a 'main Aspect' that determined the minimum level for the Spell. Since this is no longer the case, the level for your casting is the highest Aspect you want to use.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}